<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ethiopia: Fighting resumes in Tigray</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c59ff5cb8746cdf23cc892bc12c4a692a4aa96bea1c6e89c87ccf38bb1bb715</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-fighting-resumes-in-tigray/a-79394192--9abf0a9cd5c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-fighting-resumes-in-tigray/a-79394192?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rebels in northern Ethiopia have seized regional airports and engaged government troops in Afar and Amhara. Observers fear deadly clashes could expand after rebels announced a new anti-government alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>ICC convicts CAR ex-rebel leader of crimes against humanity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e781f35b0fd049e2a47531f52d2880c4311273c81ae6c64f932b86133526c7a6</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icc-convicts-car-ex-rebel-leader-of-crimes-against-humanity/a-79387178--62b2a3b09a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icc-convicts-car-ex-rebel-leader-of-crimes-against-humanity/a-79387178?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Criminal Court has found Mahamat Said Abdel Kani guilty of overseeing torture and other crimes. He headed a feared prison unit that held political prisoners.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: 11 killed in attack on house party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29d23d92f3d8ebadd1a8d2214d5ba8766f66c1302980dc743721a1c066af18aa</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:45:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-11-killed-in-attack-on-house-party/a-79382743--e4b1a2c13c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-11-killed-in-attack-on-house-party/a-79382743?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motive for the shooting in the town of KwaMakhutha near Durban, Kwa-Zulu Natal was not immediately clear. Some of the victims were known to police</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c606f30ea20ba6b5d5d3b6b3012292e7203358d542c9f44421ea4fa91a5f952</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Why gender-based violence persists in Southern Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2904473291f360b41ca813730d160b4297335bb5e7572efe2d55ea3b8f70c69</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-gender-based-violence-persists-in-southern-africa/a-79356560--3226110a275f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-gender-based-violence-persists-in-southern-africa/a-79356560?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A series of killings in South Africa has renewed scrutiny of efforts to combat violence against women. Activists say laws alone are not enough without effective implementation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Decolonizing perceptions about Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca58f5f00507f38717695eb7890eddf6009be86ec5240c5f0a774a3380c7a0cf</id><updated>2026-09-23T13:44:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178--8deea6e78a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a UN resolution alters the standard global map to reflect the continent more accurately, initiatives to decolonize African schools and a campaign to present positive developments are changing the way Africa is seen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
